@Structure
$# Dialog file structure#

  File consist of constant declaration and dialog
  definition. All lines beginning with ';' is
  comments.
   Format of constant declaration is C-like:

  #enum { [ _name_[=_value_],...] }#

  dialog defenition consist of:
  #name " _name_of_dialog_ "#        - name of dialog
  #help " _name_of_help_contents_ "# - name of help topic.
                                     "Contents" by default.

  Dialog items:
  #name id x1 y1 x2 y2 focus selected Flags DefButton Data#
  £¤¥
   #name#         - type of item
   #id#           - Id of dialog item
   #x1 y1 x2 y2#  - left top coord., width, height
   #focus#        - F/T/0/1 - input focus for item
   #selected#     - F/T number or constant (.lng) / "string"
                  number and sring may be used for History.
   #Flags#        - item  features flags and color
   #DefButton#    - F/T/0/1 - default button 
   #Data#         - Data field of item.
                  Data may have a reference form.
                   Format:
                  #%LNG% _constant name_# - reference to lng-file.
                  #[%TXT%] " _text_ "#    - Text.%TXT%-may be omitted.
                  #%REG% [%HKCU% | %HKLM%] "_reg key_" _default_#
                       #default = [%DEF% "_value_"]#
                       - Data from registry. By default used HKCU.
                         If registry key can not be read then
                         default value used.
                         #"_reg key_"# - is subkey from
                         software\far\plugins\ .
                  #%VER%# - generator version.

   Item types:

   #Types   {"TEXT","VTEXT","SINGLEBOX","DOUBLEBOX",#
            #"EDIT","PSWEDIT","FIXEDIT","BUTTON",#
            #"CHECKBOX","RADIOBUTTON"};#

   Flags (features):

   #Flag    {"DIF_COLORMASK","DIF_SETCOLOR","DIF_BOXCOLOR",#
            #"DIF_GROUP","DIF_LEFTTEXT","DIF_MOVESELECT",#
            #"DIF_SHOWAMPERSAND","DIF_CENTERGROUP",#
            #"DIF_NOBRACKETS","DIF_SEPARATOR","DIF_EDITOR",#
            #"DIF_HISTORY"};#

   #Colors   {"BLACK","BLUE","GREEN","CYAN","RED","MAGENTA",#
             #"BROWN","LIGHTGRAY","DARKGRAY","LIGHTBLUE",#
             #"LIGHTGREEN","LIGHTCYAN","LIGHTRED",#
             #"LIGHTMAGENTA","YELLOW","WHITE"};#

   #BkColors  {"BK_BLACK","BK_BLUE","BK_GREEN","BK_CYAN","BK_RED",#
             #"BK_MAGENTA","BK_BROWN","BK_LIGHTGRAY","BK_DARKGRAY",#
             #"BK_LIGHTBLUE","BK_LIGHTGREEN","BK_LIGHTCYAN",#
             #"BK_LIGHTRED","BK_LIGHTMAGENTA","BK_YELLOW","BK_WHITE"};#


  ~Dialog API~@API
  ~Back~@Contents
@Example
$# Dialog using example#

  Color select dialog using.
 This dialog was created as single file so it may be
 used as example and for real plugins.

         ...
         #DialogInit(hndDll,Info);#
          // init generator
          // using plugin dll handle and FAR API structure.

         #dlg=LoadDialog(hndDll,"color.dlg","Color Select");#
          // Loading dialog "Color Select" from 
          // file "color.dlg"

         #SetRadioStatus(dlg,1,col1);#
         #SetRadioStatus(dlg,16,col2);#
          // Set current colors.
          // dlg- dialog handler,
          // Id - group member to select group,
          // Id - item to select.

         #do{#
             #SetItemColor(dlg,243,col1+col2);#
              // Set color for "text example"
              // dlg- dialog handler,
              // Id - all items with this Id 
              // will be changed color
             #res=ShowDialog(dlg);#
              // Show dialog.
             #col1=GetRadioStatus(dlg,1);#
             #col2=GetRadioStatus(dlg,16);#
              // Get selected colors
              // Id - item select group
           #}while(res!=242 && res!=-1);#
              // repeat while dialog is not accepted 
              // or canceled.
              // 242 - Id "Ok" button.
              // -1  - Id "Cancel" button

         #if(res!=-1) color=col1+col2;#
              // if dialog was accepted
              // use new colors
          ...

  ~Dialog API~@API
  ~Back~@Contents
